FINAL INSTRUCTION

Do not confuse the amount of historical text with historical depth.

Aetheria needs history that explains how societies function, why cultures differ, how political institutions emerged, how people survived, how knowledge evolved, and how the consequences of ancient events continue to influence the modern world.

Treat history as an ongoing process of cause and effect.

Build the world from its earliest existence through its modern-day condition.

Do not skip ordinary civilization in favor of cosmic mythology.

Do not focus exclusively on powerful figures.

Develop the lives of the millions of ordinary people whose accumulated actions created the world.

The final historical record should be so comprehensive that future writers and developers can create new locations, characters, factions, quests, cultures, and historical events without having to invent their historical context from scratch.

Start by auditing the repository and identifying which of these areas already exist and which require development.

Then work systematically.

Preserve the canon.

Develop the history.

Connect the eras.

And make Aetheria feel like a real civilization that has been alive for thousands of years.